  "description": "A Trail-born Steel Shapeshifter\n\nOur modern trail hardtail with geared and single-speed abilities, Sorceress conjures a spellbinding singletrack experience wherever and whenever you summon it.\n\nLet Sorceress be your guide through steep and gnarly dirt realms; it thrives on flowy, feature-rich singletrack and techy descents.\n\nSorceress channels our modern trail geometry: a long front center, steep seat tube angle, and slack headtube angle conjure playful riding, stable footing, and efficient climbing (plus the power to levitate). And with maximized standover and room for longer dropper posts, you get less saddle interference and more space to send it.\n\nThe alchemy of Surly Natch steel tubing, tuned specifically for Sorceress, gives it a lively yet smooth ride quality. True to form, Sorceress is a shapeshifter: we worked with the wizards at SRAM to develop our new patent-pending DUH dropout system. This grants you the power to run gears with a UDH hanger or Full-Mount drivetrain or swap in a single-speed chip.\n\nWhatever trail magic you seek, Sorceress can summon it.\n\nSteel frame with modern, hard-charging trail geometry designed around a 140mm travel suspension fork for a nice balance of playfulness, efficiency, and control\n\nDUH dropout system (patent pending) allows for SRAM UDH, Full-Mount, and single-speed drivetrain setups. Complete bike comes with the DUH configuration is it sold as. DUH conversion parts sold separately.\n\nRoom for two bottles on MD–XL sizes; one bottle on XS–SM sizes\n\nInclusive standover clearance and maximized dropper post fit designed to welcome riders from 4′9″ (146cm) to 6′6″ (199cm)\n\nSRAM Eagle 90 Transmission 12-speed drivetrain for durability and smooth shifting with wide gear range\n\nSRAM DB6 4-piston hydraulic disc brakes for consistent, confident stopping power\n\nTeravail Kessel tires (29 x 2.5″ or 27.5 x 2.5″ on XS) for enhanced traction, control, and grip",
